{"type":"text","timestamp":1794368402947,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"id":"prt_1c8b0f5ec001Mu45JnAWfLylXe","messageID":"msg_1c8b0e665001Uo4B6LMbSRmlRZ","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","type":"text","text":"<think>The bash tool seems to deny commands that write outside the workspace? The first command included `mkdir -p /tmp/opencode && ls -ld /tmp/opencode` and got denied. Hmm, earlier `pip download ... -d /tmp/opencode/piptest` was also denied. Perhaps the rule checks the command string for external directory paths. OK — avoid /tmp/opencode in commands; use a workspace-local directory like /workspace/.tmp for testing.\n\nNote: pip download to a workspace dir should work if pip has network/cache access.\n\nLet me create a venv in /workspace/.venv for local testing (and remove it later or leave it, it's excluded by .dockerignore; but git status would show it — there's no .gitignore, so I'd better delete it before finishing, or add a .gitignore. Adding a .gitignore is reasonable and helpful: .venv, __pycache__, data/, node_modules, frontend/dist).\n\nLet's try installing flask locally.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794368402924,"end":1794368402943}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794368407803,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c8b0f028742a873a243e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"timeout 300 python3 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install -q --disable-pip-version-check flask==3.1.3 gunicorn==26.2.0 2>&1 | tail -5; .venv/bin/python -c \"import flask, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\"","workdir":"/workspace"},"output":"<string>:1: DeprecationWarning: The '__version__' attribute is deprecated and will be removed in Flask 3.2. Use feature detection or 'importlib.metadata.version(\"flask\")' instead.\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\n                                                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nAttributeError: module 'werkzeug' has no attribute '__version__'\n","metadata":{"output":"<string>:1: DeprecationWarning: The '__version__' attribute is deprecated and will be removed in Flask 3.2. Use feature detection or 'importlib.metadata.version(\"flask\")' instead.\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\n                                                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nAttributeError: module 'werkzeug' has no attribute '__version__'\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"timeout 300 python3 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install -q --disable-pip-version-check flask==3.1.3 gunicorn==26.2.0 2>&1 | tail -5; .venv/bin/python -c \"import flask, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\"","time":{"start":1794368402934,"end":1794368407750}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c8b0f5ef001tMVTIWVuQXny8a","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","messageID":"msg_1c8b0e665001Uo4B6LMbSRmlRZ"}}
