{"type":"text","timestamp":1794368591515,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"id":"prt_1c8b3d687001a6w2aEJtAsRsR2","messageID":"msg_1c8b3b864001RG0oagClZsPusL","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","type":"text","text":"<think>Now let me test the backend locally. Start gunicorn (or the flask dev server) with ADMIN_PASSWORD set and run a test script.\n\nLet me write a test script in /workspace/scripts? Or use a python script in /workspace/.tmp. I'll create /workspace/scripts/smoke_test.py — hmm, should I keep it in the repo? It's useful for verification but the task doesn't require it. I'll put it in a temp location within the workspace and delete later, or keep it as a dev script. I'll create it under /workspace/.tmp/ (gitignored via .gitignore I add).\n\nLet me first run the server and do a quick curl test.\n\nNote the DB path: /workspace/data/leaderboard.db (APP_ROOT = /workspace). Good — matches \"./data\" relative to the working directory /app in the container.\n\nLet me start gunicorn from the backenddir.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794368591495,"end":1794368591512}}}
