        if not check_password_hash(row[\"password_hash\"], ADMIN_PASSWORD):\n+            db.execute(\n+                \"UPDATE users SET password_hash = ?, is_admin = 1 WHERE id = ?\",\n+                (\n+                    generate_password_hash(ADMIN_PASSWORD, method=PASSWORD_HASH_METHOD),\n+                    row[\"id\"],\n+                ),\n+            )\n+            db.execute(\"DELETE FROM tokens WHERE user_id = ?\", (row[\"id\"],))\n+            db.commit()\n+        else:\n+            db.execute(\"UPDATE users SET is_admin = 1 WHERE id = ?\", (row[\"id\"],))\n+            db.commit()\n+        return int(row[\"id\"])\n+    finally:\n+        db.close()\n \n \n def disable_admin_account() -> None:\n     \"\"\"Admin sign-in is switched off: no admin rights and no live tokens.\"\"\"\n \n     db = connect()\n-    row = db.execute(\n-        \"SELECT id AS id FROM users WHERE username = ? COLLATE NOCASE\", (ADMIN_USERNAME,)\n-    ).fetchone()\n-    if row is None:\n-        return\n-    db.execute(\"UPDATE users SET is_admin = 0 WHERE id = ?\", (row[\"id\"],))\n-    db.execute(\"DELETE FROM tokens WHERE user_id = ?\", (row[\"id\"],))\n-    db.commit()\n+    try:\n+        row = db.execute(\n+            \"SELECT id AS id FROM users WHERE username = ? COLLATE NOCASE\", (ADMIN_USERNAME,)\n+        ).fetchone()\n+        if row is None:\n+            return\n+        db.execute(\"UPDATE users SET is_admin = 0 WHERE id = ?\", (row[\"id\"],))\n+        db.execute(\"DELETE FROM tokens WHERE user_id = ?\", (row[\"id\"],))\n+        db.commit()\n+    finally:\n+        db.close()\n \n \n def setup_admin() -> None:\n     if ADMIN_PASSWORD:\n","additions":45,"deletions":30},"truncated":false},"title":"backend/api.py","time":{"start":1794368631307,"end":1794368631360}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c8b47202001MFupe2pvf7z7rG","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","messageID":"msg_1c8b43c8a001oa6tK2pveeDF6w"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794368631406,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"id":"prt_1c8b472420016wwt1oWQj31g0u","reason":"tool-calls","messageID":"msg_1c8b43c8a001oa6tK2pveeDF6w","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":44536,"input":723,"output":841,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"write":0,"read":42972}},"cost":0}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794368636797,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"id":"prt_1c8b4875f001jHypxhiHEUBIoi","messageID":"msg_1c8b4724e001zRFcplcrznopo6","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794368636797,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"id":"prt_1c8b48762001fxLI8G02Zfsu8f","messageID":"msg_1c8b4724e001zRFcplcrznopo6","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","type":"text","text":"<think>Also `login` calls `ensure_admin_user()` which now opens its own connection — but login is inside a request with a `g.db` connection. SQLite WAL allows multiple connections; the ensure_admin_user connection commits changes; the request's connection may hold a read snapshot... In WAL mode with the request connection not in a transaction, it should see the new data. But there's a subtlety: the request's `get_db()` connection might have an open read transaction from a prior SELECT in the same request (sqlite3 module in Python doesn't start transactions for SELECTs by default — autocommit mode for reads). Actually Python's sqlite3 module with default isolation_level=\"\" begins a transaction before DML (INSERT/UPDATE), not before SELECT. So reads happen in autocommit → each SELECT sees the latest committed data. Good.\n\nBut wait: in `login`, before `ensure_admin_user()`, I called `get_db()` and executed a SELECT (only in the non-admin branch). For the admin branch, no SELECT happens before ensure_admin_user. Fine.\n\nHowever, there's a potential issue: ensure_admin_user's UPDATE/DELETE via a separate connection while the request connection has an open write transaction → \"database is locked\". In login, the admin branch: `issue_token` does an INSERT on the request connection (commits immediately). Fine.\n\nLet me now restart the server and test.\n\nAlso: `init_db()` and `setup_admin()` run at import; with gunicorn multiple workers, each worker runs init → concurrent schema creation could race. `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` with WAL + busy_timeout should be OK.\n\nLet me restart and test.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794368636770,"end":1794368636793}}}
