{"type":"text","timestamp":1794368773430,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"id":"prt_1c8b69d21001QPVgocja9cN0Gc","messageID":"msg_1c8b65cbb001G2bhQuwdNHKkQO","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","type":"text","text":"<think>The server started (the health check worked). The shell hung because the background process keeps the shell open. I need to run background processes with output redirected and `disown`/`nohup` so the shell returns. The `> log 2>&1 &` should have detached... but the shell waits for the pipe. Let me use `nohup ... &` with stdin redirected from /dev/null, and add `exec 1>&-`? A common trick: `setsid cmd > log 2>&1 < /dev/null &`.\n\nLet me check whether the server is still running and then write a smoke test script.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794368773409,"end":1794368773425}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794368773502,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c8b698df706f841f71d1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"pgrep -af gunicorn | head -5; curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8111/api/health; echo"},"output":"4650 /usr/bin/bash -c pgrep -af gunicorn | head -5; curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8111/api/health; echo\n\n","metadata":{"output":"4650 /usr/bin/bash -c pgrep -af gunicorn | head -5; curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8111/api/health; echo\n\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"pgrep -af gunicorn | head -5; curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8111/api/health; echo","time":{"start":1794368773417,"end":1794368773467}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c8b69d240019gbZG6BpYMZM7M","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","messageID":"msg_1c8b65cbb001G2bhQuwdNHKkQO"}}
