{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794368967470,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"id":"prt_1c8b9930d001VaYnk0zv3Pf2XS","messageID":"msg_1c8b95754001GjPRm10LGBnRbV","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794368967471,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"id":"prt_1c8b99311001sD3fxfCyOq51PF","messageID":"msg_1c8b95754001GjPRm10LGBnRbV","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","type":"text","text":"<think>The versions installed use `^` ranges for the new ones. The existing deps are pinned exactly (react 19.3.1, vite 8.3.5). For consistency with the repo style (pinned), let me pin the new devDeps exactly: \"@tailwindcss/vite\": \"4.3.5\", \"tailwindcss\": \"4.3.5\", \"typescript\": \"5.9.3\", \"@types/react\": \"19.3.0\", \"@types/react-dom\": \"19.3.0\".\n\nThe lock file will still resolve to those exact versions since the package-lock records the resolved versions; but `npm ci` verifies that the lock satisfies package.json. With exact pins it's cleaner.\n\nLet me edit package.json and re-run npm install to sync the lock.\n\nAlso add a \"typecheck\" script: \"tsc --noEmit\" and a tsconfig.json.\n\nLet me write tsconfig.json for the frontend:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": true,\n    \"lib\": [\"ES2022\", \"DOM\", \"DOM.Iterable\"],\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"verbatimModuleSyntax\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"noUnusedLocals\": true,\n    \"noUnusedParameters\": true,\n    \"noFallthroughCasesInSwitch\": true\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"src\"]\n}\n```\n\nWith \"verbatimModuleSyntax\": true, type imports must use `import type`. I'll be careful.\n\nLet me now write the frontend code.\n\nFiles:\n- frontend/index.html (update title)\n- frontend/vite.config.ts (add tailwind plugin)\n- frontend/tsconfig.json, tsconfig.node.json? A single tsconfig is enough for `tsc --noEmit` on src. But vite.config.ts is outside `include` — fine, but then tsc doesn't check it. I'll include vite.config.ts in a separate tsconfig.node.json. Keep it simple: one tsconfig with include: [\"src\", \"vite.config.ts\"]? vite.config.ts needs node types (not installed). I'll just include \"src\" and add \"types\": [\"vite/client\"].\n\nLet me write the app.\n\n**src/types.ts**\n```ts\nexport interface Score {\n  id: number;\n  score: number;\n  achieved_at: string;\n  is_hidden: boolean;\n  player: string;\n}\n\nexport interface LeaderboardItem {\n  rank: number;\n  player: string;\n  score: number;\n  achieved_at: string;\n}\n\nexport interface LeaderboardResponse { items: LeaderboardItem[]; total: number; }\nexport interface MyScoresResponse { items: Score[]; best_score: number | null; }\nexport interface AdminScoresResponse { items: Score[]; total: number; page: number; page_size: number; }\nexport interface SubmittedScore extends Score { rank: number | null; personal_best: boolean; }\nexport interface User { id: number; username: string; is_admin: boolean; }\nexport type Period = \"all\" | \"week\" | \"today\";\n```\n\n**src/api.ts** — client + token storage.\n\n**src/App.tsx** — orchestrates.\n\nComponents:\n- AuthPanel: tabs \"Sign in\" / \"Create account\", username/password inputs, submit, error display. On success: set token, fetch /api/auth/me.\n- Header: app title, signed-in username + role badge + Sign out button.\n- Leaderboard: period tabs (All time / This week / Today), search input, refresh button, table with rank/player/score/date; top-3 marking (medal for rank 1-3); the signed-in player's row highlighted.\n- ScoreForm: number input, submit; shows \"New personal best!\" message + new rank.\n- MyScores: best score + recent submissions list.\n- AdminPanel: table of all scores with hide/show button + pagination.\n\nDesign: dark slate theme with an amber/indigo accent. Let me write good-looking Tailwind markup.\n\nLet me write the code now. I'll use a shared `formatDate` helper for dates.\n\nFor the period tabs, the active tab gets a highlighted style.\n\nFor the refresh button: refetch the leaderboard (and my scores).\n\nSearch: a text input with a \"Search\" button and also live filtering on Enter. I'll implement: controlled input `search`, and a `appliedSearch` state that triggers the fetch. Live search with a debounce is nicer; I'll debounce by 300ms.\n\nAlso note: when the signed-in user submits a score, refresh the leaderboard and my scores.\n\nLet me write the files.\n\nOne more: the frontend must handle the 401 case (expired token) → clear the token and show the sign-in form.\n\nLet me write api.ts:\n\n```ts\nconst TOKEN_KEY = \"leaderboard_token\";\n\nexport class ApiError extends Error {\n  status: number;\n  constructor(message: string, status: number) { super(message); this.status = status; }\n}\n\nexport function getToken(): string | null {\n  try { return window.localStorage.getItem(TOKEN_KEY); } catch { return null; }\n}\nexport function setToken(token: string | null) {\n  try {\n    if (token) window.localStorage.setItem(TOKEN_KEY, token);\n    else window.localStorage.removeItem(TOKEN_KEY);\n  } catch { /* ignore */ }\n}\n\nasync function request<T>(path: string, init: { method?: string; body?: unknown } = {}): Promise<T> {\n  const headers: Record<string, string> = {};\n  if (init.body !== undefined) headers[\"Content-Type\"] = \"application/json\";\n  const token = getToken();\n  if (token) headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;\n  const response = await fetch(path, {\n    method: init.method ?? \"GET\",\n    headers,\n    body: init.body === undefined ? undefined : JSON.stringify(init.body),\n  });\n  const text = await response.text();\n  let payload: unknown = null;\n  if (text) { try { payload = JSON.parse(text); } catch { payload = null; } }\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    const message = (payload as {error?: string} | null)?.error ?? `Request failed (${response.status})`;\n    throw new ApiError(message, response.status);\n  }\n  return payload as T;\n}\n```\n\nAlso a `query(params)` helper.\n\nNow App.tsx structure:\n\n```tsx\nexport default function App() {\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);\n  const [booting, setBooting] = useState(true);\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nOn mount: if a token exists, fetch /api/auth/me → set user; else null.\n\nAfter sign-in: setToken(token); fetch me → setUser; refresh data.\n\nLet me write the components with props.\n\nI'll write it now. Let me be careful with TypeScript strictness (noUnusedLocals etc.).\n\nLet me write allfiles.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794368967441,"end":1794368967465}}}
