{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794369014959,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"id":"prt_1c8ba4c7e001FffWlmm1w2M7z4","messageID":"msg_1c8ba24d00018m1J7Ywl13uIih","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794369014959,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"id":"prt_1c8ba4c82001nL1EsnpdklUQ67","messageID":"msg_1c8ba24d00018m1J7Ywl13uIih","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","type":"text","text":"<think>Now the components. Let me create a shared `format.ts` helper for dates and rank styling.\n\nsrc/lib/format.ts:\n```ts\nexport function formatDate(value: string): string {\n  const date = new Date(value);\n  if (Number.isNaN(date.getTime())) return value;\n  return date.toLocaleString(undefined, { dateStyle: \"medium\", timeStyle: \"short\" });\n}\nexport function formatNumber(value: number): string { return value.toLocaleString(); }\n```\n\nComponents:\n\n1. `src/components/AuthPanel.tsx`\n```tsx\ninterface Props { onSignedIn: (user: User) => void; }\n```\nTabs: signin/register. Fields: username, password. Error display. Loading state.\n\n2. `src/components/Leaderboard.tsx`\nProps: period, onPeriodChange, search, onSearchChange, items, total, loading, currentUsername, onRefresh.\n\nActually, let me keep the data fetching in App and pass props down. Or let each component fetch? Simpler: App holds leaderboard state and passes down.\n\n3. `src/components/ScoreForm.tsx`\nProps: onSubmitted(result), user.\n\nActually let me have ScoreForm call api.submitScore and then call `onSubmitted(result)`; App refreshes the leaderboard.\n\n4. `src/components/MyScores.tsx`: props { items, bestScore, onRefresh }.\n\n5. `src/components/AdminPanel.tsx`: props { onChanged } — it fetches its own data with pagination. Let me have it fetch internally to keep App simpler, with a refresh trigger.\n\nLet me write the App:\n\n```tsx\nexport default function App() {\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);\n  const [ready, setReady] = useState(false);\n  const [period, setPeriod] = useState<Period>(\"all\");\n  const [search, setSearch] = useState(\"\");\n  const [appliedSearch, setAppliedSearch] = useState(\"\");\n  const [board, setBoard] = useState<LeaderboardResponse>({ items: [], total: 0 });\n  const [boardLoading, setBoardLoading] = useState(false);\n  const [boardError, setBoardError] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  const [myScores, setMyScores] = useState<MyScoresResponse>({ items: [], best_score: null });\n  const [notice, setNotice] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nBootstrapping: on mount, if a token exists → api.me() → setUser; else null. Then load the leaderboard regardless.\n\nloadBoard: uses period + appliedSearch.\n\nDebounced search: useEffect on `search` with a 300ms timeout → setAppliedSearch(search).\n\nloadMyScores: only when user.\n\nLet me write it all now. I'll write the components with clean Tailwind classes.\n\nDesign tokens:\n- Background: bg-slate-950 with a subtle radial gradient.\n- Cards: bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-800 rounded-2xl shadow.\n- Accent: amber-400 (trophy), indigo-500.\n- Top three: rank 1 → amber-300/amber-500 medal with a crown emoji? Use text badges: 🥇🥈🥉? Emojis are only used if the user requests... \"Only use emojis if the user explicitly requests it. Avoid adding emojis to files unless asked.\" So no emojis. Use colored badges: rank 1 → bg-amber-400 text-slate-950, rank 2 → bg-slate-300, rank 3 → bg-amber-700.\n\nI'll mark the top three with a colored rank badge + a subtle row tint (amber-950/40 etc.).\n\nLet me write the code.\n\nFor the \"top three marked\" requirement, the rank badge colors make it clear.\n\nLet me write AuthPanel.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794369014914,"end":1794369014947}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794369015015,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_01a1c8ba46a777c69deb9c62","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"export function formatDate(value: string): string {\n  const date = new Date(value);\n  if (Number.isNaN(date.getTime())) {\n    return value;\n  }\n  return date.toLocaleString(undefined, {\n    year: \"numeric\",\n    month: \"short\",\n    day: \"numeric\",\n    hour: \"2-digit\",\n    minute: \"2-digit\",\n  });\n}\n\nexport function formatNumber(value: number): string {\n  return value.toLocaleString();\n}\n\nexport function errorMessage(error: unknown): string {\n  if (error instanceof Error) {\n    return error.message;\n  }\n  return \"Something went wrong\";\n}\n","filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/lib/format.ts"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/frontend/src/lib/format.ts","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/src/lib/format.ts","time":{"start":1794369014934,"end":1794369014973}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c8ba4c8d001uGFBin5PmNz0Li","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","messageID":"msg_1c8ba24d00018m1J7Ywl13uIih"}}
