{"type":"text","timestamp":1794369256296,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"id":"prt_1c8bdfb5a001tlRkwo9WMh0kmQ","messageID":"msg_1c8bdbd6b001ggYgQ81ed4azF8","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","type":"text","text":"<think>Installed. Note: esbuild's postinstall wasn't run — vitest needs esbuild's binary. Let me check if it works; if not, run `npm approve-scripts` or `npm rebuild esbuild`.\n\nLet me write a UI test file. I'll put it in frontend/src/__tests__/app.test.tsx (temporary; I'll delete it later, or maybe keep it — keeping tests is good practice, but the task doesn't require it and the extra devDeps slow the Docker build. Let me decide later; first make it work).\n\nTest plan:\n1. Render <App /> with fetch mocked to return the leaderboard → expect the leaderboard rows to render.\n2. Sign in flow: fill the username/password, click Sign in → expect the header to show the username and the score form to appear.\n3. Submit a score → expect \"New personal best!\" and the rank.\n4. Admin: with is_admin true → expect the admin panel and hide/show buttons.\n\nI need to mock global.fetch. I'll write a simple mock that routes based on URL and method.\n\nLet me write the test file.\n\nVitest config: I'll add a `vitest.config.ts`? Vitest can read vite.config.ts, but the tailwind plugin might interfere in tests (it should be fine). I need `environment: \"jsdom\"`. I'll add a separate `vitest.config.ts` file with the react plugin and jsdom env. Since vite.config.ts has the proxy and tailwind plugin, using it as the vitest config might work too, but the environment needs to be jsdom → set via the test script: `vitest run --environment jsdom`.\n\nLet me create the test file and run `npx vitest run --environment jsdom`.\n\nFor the fetch mock, the API returns JSON; my api.ts calls response.text() then JSON.parse. So the mock must return an object with `text()`, `ok`, `status`.\n\nLet me write a helper:\n\n```ts\nfunction jsonResponse(data: unknown, status = 200) {\n  return {\n    ok: status >= 200 && status < 300,\n    status,\n    text: async () => JSON.stringify(data),\n  } as unknown as Response;\n}\n```\n\nMock fetch:\n```ts\nconst state = { scores: [...], users: ... };\nglobal.fetch = vi.fn(async (input: RequestInfo | URL, init?: RequestInit) => { ... })\n```\n\nLet me write the tests.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794369256282,"end":1794369256292}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794369256317,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_01a1c8bdd0c671399f100500","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"import { cleanup, fireEvent, render, screen, waitFor } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport App from \"../App\";\n\ntype Handler = (path: string, method: string, body: unknown) => { status: number; data: unknown };\n\nlet handler: Handler;\nlet requests: { path: string; method: string; body: unknown }[] = [];\n\nfunction jsonResponse(data: unknown, status = 200) {\n  return {\n    ok: status >= 200 && status < 300,\n    status,\n    text: async () => JSON.stringify(data),\n  } as unknown as Response;\n}\n\nbeforeEach(() => {\n  requests = [];\n  localStorage.clear();\n  handler = () => ({ status: 200, data: {} });\n  global.fetch = vi.fn(async (input: RequestInfo | URL, init?: RequestInit) => {\n    const path = String(input);\n    const method = init?.method ?? \"GET\";\n    const body = init?.body ? JSON.parse(String(init.body)) : undefined;\n    requests.push({ path, method, body });\n    const result = handler(path, method, body);\n    return jsonResponse(result.data, result.status);\n  }) as unknown as typeof fetch;\n});\n\nafterEach(() => {\n  cleanup();\n});\n\nconst board = {\n  items: [\n    { rank: 1, player: \"zed\", score: 900, achieved_at: \"2026-01-02T10:00:00Z\" },\n    { rank: 2, player: \"alice\", score: 500, achieved_at: \"2026-01-02T11:00:00Z\" },\n  ],\n  total: 2,\n};\n\ndescribe(\"leaderboard app\", () => {\n  it(\"shows the leaderboard to anonymous visitors\", async () => {\n    handler = (path) =>\n      path.startsWith(\"/api/leaderboard\")\n        ? { status: 200, data: board }\n        : { status: 200, data: {} };\n\n    render(<App />);\n\n    expect(await screen.findByText(\"zed\")).toBeTruthy();\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"alice\")).toBeTruthy();\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Sign in\")).toBeTruthy();\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: /create account/i })).toBeTruthy();\n  });\n\n  it(\"signs a player in and submits a score\", async () => {\n    const tokens: Record<string, string> = { alice: \"alice-token\" };\n    handler = (path, method) => {\n      if (path === \"/api/auth/login\" && method === \"POST\") {\n        return { status: 200, data: { token: tokens.alice } };\n      }\n      if (path === \"/api/auth/me\") {\n        return { status: 200, data: { id: 2, username: \"alice\", is_admin: false } };\n      }\n      if (path === \"/api/scores\" && method === \"POST\") {\n        return {\n          status: 201,\n          data: {\n            id: 9,\n            score: 750,\n            achieved_at: \"2026-01-02T12:00:00Z\",\n            is_hidden: false,\n            player: \"alice\",\n            rank: 1,\n            personal_best: true,\n          },\n        };\n      }\n      if (path === \"/api/scores\") {\n        return {\n          status: 200,\n          data: {\n            items: [\n              {\n                id: 9,\n                score: 750,\n                achieved_at: \"2026-01-02T12:00:00Z\",\n                is_hidden: false,\n                player: \"alice\",\n              },\n            ],\n            best_score: 750,\n          },\n        };\n      }\n      if (path.startsWith(\"/api/leaderboard\")) {\n        return { status: 200, data: board };\n      }\n      return { status: 200, data: {} };\n    };\n\n    render(<App />);\n\n    fireEvent.change(await screen.findByLabelText(\"Username\"), { target: { value: \"alice\" } });\n    fireEvent.change(screen.getByLabelText(\"Password\"), { target: { value: \"pw\" } });\n    fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\" }));\n\n    expect(await screen.findByText(\"alice\")).toBeTruthy();\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: /sign out/i })).toBeTruthy();\n\n    fireEvent.change(await screen.findByLabelText(\"Score\"), { target: { value: \"750\" } });\n    fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: /save score/i }));\n\n    expect(await screen.findByText(\"New personal best!\")).toBeTruthy();\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"#1\")).toBeTruthy();\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"750\")).toBeTruthy();\n\n    const submit = requests.find((r) => r.method === \"POST\" && r.path === \"/api/scores\");\n    expect(submit?.body).toEqual({ score: 750 });\n  });\n\n  it(\"switches period tabs and searches for a player\", async () => {\n    handler = (path) =>\n      path.startsWith(\"/api/leaderboard\")\n        ? { status: 200, data: board }\n        : { status: 200, data: {} };\n\n    render(<App />);\n    await screen.findByText(\"zed\");\n\n    fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"This week\" }));\n    await waitFor(() => {\n      const calls = requests.filter((r) => r.path.startsWith(\"/api/leaderboard\"));\n      expect(calls.some((c) => c.path.includes(\"period=week\"))).toBe(true);\n    });\n\n    fireEvent.change(screen.getByPlaceholderText(\"Search player…\"), {\n      target: { value: \"ali\" },\n    });\n    await waitFor(() => {\n      const calls = requests.filter((r) => r.path.startsWith(\"/api/leaderboard\"));\n      expect(calls.some((c) => c.path.includes(\"player=ali\"))).toBe(true);\n    });\n  });\n\n  it(\"lets the admin hide a score\", async () => {\n    handler = (path, method) => {\n      if (path === \"/api/auth/login\") {\n        return { status: 200, data: { token: \"admin-token\" } };\n      }\n      if (path === \"/api/auth/me\") {\n        return { status: 200, data: { id: 1, username: \"admin\", is_admin: true } };\n      }\n      if (path.startsWith(\"/api/admin/scores\") && method === \"GET\") {\n        return {\n          status: 200,\n          data: {\n            items: [\n              {\n                id: 3,\n                score: 999999,\n                achieved_at: \"2026-01-02T12:00:00Z\",\n                is_hidden: false,\n                player: \"cheater\",\n              },\n            ],\n            total: 1,\n            page: 1,\n            page_size: 20,\n          },\n        };\n      }\n      if (path.startsWith(\"/api/admin/scores\") && method === \"POST\") {\n        return { status: 200, data: { id: 3, is_hidden: true } };\n      }\n      if (path.startsWith(\"/api/leaderboard\")) {\n        return { status: 200, data: board };\n      }\n      if (path === \"/api/scores\") {\n        return { status: 200, data: { items: [], best_score: null } };\n      }\n      return { status: 200, data: {} };\n    };\n\n    render(<App />);\n\n    fireEvent.change(await screen.findByLabelText(\"Username\"), { target: { value: \"admin\" } });\n    fireEvent.change(screen.getByLabelText(\"Password\"), { target: { value: \"pw\" } });\n    fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\" }));\n\n    expect(await screen.findByText(/admin · all scores/i)).toBeTruthy();\n    expect(await screen.findByText(\"999999\")).toBeTruthy();\n\n    fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Hide\" }));\n    await waitFor(() => {\n      expect(\n        requests.some((r) => r.method === \"POST\" && r.path === \"/api/admin/scores/3/toggle\"),\n      ).toBe(true);\n    });\n  });\n});\n","filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/__tests__/app.test.tsx"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/frontend/src/__tests__/app.test.tsx","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/src/__tests__/app.test.tsx","time":{"start":1794369256289,"end":1794369256299}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c8bdfb5c001SEqjlxTlrd0r8q","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","messageID":"msg_1c8bdbd6b001ggYgQ81ed4azF8"}}
