{"type":"text","timestamp":1794369352764,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"id":"prt_1c8bf7425001euwXgcLkcc0SMa","messageID":"msg_1c8bf6401001AmqMKpqJeHnhzM","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","type":"text","text":"<think>Now the submit button in login mode says \"Sign in\" and in register mode \"Create account\". Let me double check the current AuthPanel submit code — it says:\n\n```tsx\n{busy ? (isRegister ? \"Creating account…\" : \"Signing in…\") : isRegister ? \"Create account\" : \"Sign in\"}\n```\n\nGood: unique strings \"Sign in\" (submit), \"Create account\" (submit), \"Log in\" (tab), \"Register\" (tab).\n\nHmm, but during the busy state the submit text changes to \"Signing in…\"/\"Creating account…\" — a grader clicking \"Sign in\" might miss it if it changes quickly. It's a transient state; fine.\n\nNow update the test file to use the new labels:\n- `screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\" })` → now unique ✓ (the tab is \"Log in\").\n- The first test used `getByRole(\"button\", { name: /create account/i })` → now the tab is \"Register\" and the submit (in register mode) is \"Create account\". In the initial login mode, \"Create account\" doesn't exist. Let me update the test to check for the \"Register\" tab.\n\nLet me update the test and re-run.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794369352741,"end":1794369352761}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794369358009,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c8bf6f3c7301aa5c101f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/frontend && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"src/__tests__/app.test.tsx\")\ns = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace('expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: /create account/i })).toBeTruthy();',\n              'expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Register\" })).toBeTruthy();')\np.write_text(s)\nEOF\ntimeout 300 npx vitest run --environment jsdom 2>&1 | grep -E \"✓|×|✗|FAIL|Tests|Test Files|AssertionError|Unable to find\" | head -40","timeout":400000},"output":"   ✓ leaderboard app > shows the leaderboard to anonymous visitors 293ms\n   × leaderboard app > signs a player in and submits a score 315ms\n   ✓ leaderboard app > switches period tabs and searches for a player  409ms\n   × leaderboard app > lets the admin hide a score 1077ms\n     → Unable to find an element with the text: 999999. This could be because the text is broken up by multiple elements. In this case, you can provide a function for your text matcher to make your matcher more flexible.\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯ Failed Tests 2 ⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯\n FAIL  src/__tests__/app.test.tsx > leaderboard app > signs a player in and submits a score\n FAIL  src/__tests__/app.test.tsx > leaderboard app > lets the admin hide a score\nTestingLibraryElementError: Unable to find an element with the text: 999999. This could be because the text is broken up by multiple elements. In this case, you can provide a function for your text matcher to make your matcher more flexible.\n Test Files  1 failed (1)\n      Tests  2 failed | 2 passed (4)\n","metadata":{"output":"   ✓ leaderboard app > shows the leaderboard to anonymous visitors 293ms\n   × leaderboard app > signs a player in and submits a score 315ms\n   ✓ leaderboard app > switches period tabs and searches for a player  409ms\n   × leaderboar