{"type":"text","timestamp":1794369375653,"sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","part":{"id":"prt_1c8bfcd8e001mtr3nEhGMDMVQJ","messageID":"msg_1c8bfb66f001gZet97aJwd837z","sessionID":"ses_e3750b618ffeN46LwuGHIvwVmz","type":"text","text":"<think>Both failures are due to my test's overly loose assertions (multiple \"750\" elements, and \"999,999\" with a separator). The app works. Let me fix the assertions:\n- Use `getAllByText(\"750\").length` > 0 or use `getByText(\"#1\")` (unique?) — \"#1\" appears in the score form result; the leaderboard shows rank \"1\" in a badge (not \"#1\"). So \"#1\" is unique ✓ (it already passed).\n- Replace `screen.getByText(\"750\")` with `getAllByText(\"750\")[0]`.\n- Replace \"999999\" with \"999,999\".\n\nLet me apply andre-run.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794369375630,"end":1794369375649}}}
